#uuid "b3f10959-4573-5095-94c3-45484a99ec71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487909} {:answer/id #uuid "c1157647-1f2f-5647-ba3c-a7d0af45f9e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487930} {:answer/id #uuid "de33f900-f0ee-54b2-86e2-8e0dbacd4624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1157647-1f2f-5647-ba3c-a7d0af45f9e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487930} :answer-field/id #uuid "7711e40c-c300-5c27-b9a0-b4edcb7004f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71992831-f081-5b4f-8e3b-b908eab2b80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487795} {:answer/id #uuid "cde51993-46ba-5136-b04b-e60fd29425c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71992831-f081-5b4f-8e3b-b908eab2b80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487795} :answer-field/id #uuid "8228ce6d-4eae-56db-adb9-39e0b92fe3e4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d48b0cc5-05e8-55c3-b441-64611554a8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-253553" :question/problem "Consider the set $B=[-1,2).$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $inf(B).$\n\nThe infimum of $B$ is the {{field-1}} of $B.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $B$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\le -1$ is smaller than or equal to the elements of $B.$ Thus, the set $(-\\infty ,-1]$ contains only lower bounds of $B.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x>-1$ is **not** a lower bound of $B.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $B$ that is smaller than $x$ for any $x>-1.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-1]$ is the set of lower bounds of $B,$ and\n\n$$\ninf(B)=max(-\\infty ,-1]=-1.\n$$\n\nNotice that $-1$ is also the minimum of $B.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of $B$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $B.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $B$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\le -1\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $inf(B)=-1\\in B.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162158 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe2b2c0-23a0-5bd0-8bc7-c12139820b61" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b722803a-370b-5cc6-8dec-952c663984fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160503} {:answer/id #uuid "128ee1a2-ad98-5075-846f-b8cbe5627a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{7}{4}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487604} {:answer/id #uuid "7d320ab4-e7ea-5b1a-9b1e-fcd8c46760b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=1\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487808} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2c2649-8169-5a93-bf6e-55c2f61519ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{7}{4}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488011} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb9e03b-cb3d-5a8d-9ae0-14d4a6eba10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=1\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "128ee1a2-ad98-5075-846f-b8cbe5627a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{7}{4}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487604} :answer-field/id #uuid "fce77323-ea42-5087-8e83-d953a7ffc6f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4afd4c3a-6ec4-5cdc-b8ec-af8373f2b829" :question/math-academy-id "q-253840" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{1+3{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=1+3{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/19/198c3d6737439fcfa204926394b317aae0026502b5eaacb9e2f0429941f23db3.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing and converges to $1.$ The maximum of $A$ is \n\n$$\nmax(A)={a}_{1}=1+3{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{1}=\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $x\\ge {a}_{1}$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $x<{a}_{1}$ cannot be an upper bound because ${a}_{1},$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $x.$\n\nTherefore, $[\\frac{7}{4},\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[\\frac{7}{4},\\infty )=\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\frac{7}{4}$ is the maximum of $A.$ Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nsup(A)=\\frac{7}{4}\\in A.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d3c0fd-5ae1-5420-a4ca-ca1916926180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d3c0fd-5ae1-5420-a4ca-ca1916926180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487701} :answer-field/id #uuid "113dae54-601d-51b2-b64c-2c10aa2e3a1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63e6c2b8-b883-58eb-b129-69256fecf5f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-253853" :question/problem "![](images/73/73d739c3d2e4c6bc9d296136ef6f17e7fa0bf565aa4c8c4712e54df4e952935f.png)\n\nWhat is the infimum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a function is the infimum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=[-1,3].$\n\nTo find the infimum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\le -1$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y>-1$ is **not** a lower bound of $A$ because $-1,$ an element of $A,$ is smaller than $y.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-1]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=inf(A)=max(-\\infty ,-1]=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cc0bbd3-ba25-5fd0-9b64-f33746e77c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487716} {:answer/id #uuid "712bb123-f03c-5bbb-9049-2ae6f776e6a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487793} {:answer/id #uuid "72410791-1a6d-5c90-b6f7-7312d8ca4da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487796} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8029f6-c90e-5c0c-bfd4-81655fc8e004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487836} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ab285f-819b-5164-92e2-6ee90a76aa82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d8029f6-c90e-5c0c-bfd4-81655fc8e004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487836} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3798da6-3e26-54e4-8f7c-6af936e37df8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28cb24da-7ead-51cb-82fe-c700e5c2c25f" :question/math-academy-id "q-253865" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e39b8db15f47b0c07efec1b364f6fda7b3b7991ba13d71125505b1172937888.png)\n\nWhat is the infimum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n$\\,{inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a function is the infimum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nTo find the infimum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, $A$ has no lower bounds. We can always find an element $x$ such that $f(x)$ is smaller than $y$ for any $y.$ \n\nTherefore, ${inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)$ $=-\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67197de5-74fe-5dc0-abe6-0952b996a82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67197de5-74fe-5dc0-abe6-0952b996a82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487773} :answer-field/id #uuid "42f7eabb-2484-504e-a47e-b134986a6e92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ddf4ec2c-4f4d-56c1-bc14-78cfd2f52940" :question/math-academy-id "q-253895" :question/problem "![](images/50/50b52da574101dfca7c620411a446f2c5f3ef41242186ca38da072e140019024.png)\n\nWhat is the supremum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-2,3].$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 3$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<3$ cannot be an upper bound of $A$ because $3,$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $y.$\n\nTherefore, $[3,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[3,\\infty )=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4649783b-3436-55a5-b779-1ca3de17c535" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2af8039-a78b-5fde-b644-dab8ea6d11a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2af8039-a78b-5fde-b644-dab8ea6d11a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487936} :answer-field/id #uuid "d47acad2-139e-5bc5-9fa6-bc7c2c008592" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56f49ac3-e6b5-56aa-af36-053b89a652ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-253900" :question/problem "![](images/40/40c6f3bbfcbf08db07501076a43ba011da20c57c70865ec2700334d560936eae.png)\n\nWhat is the infimum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a function is the infimum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-1,2].$\n\nTo find the infimum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\le -1$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y>-1$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $y$ for any $y>-1.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-1]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=inf(A)=max(-\\infty ,-1]=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162158 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe2b2c0-23a0-5bd0-8bc7-c12139820b61" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ac9b3db-343c-58f0-83db-0523448093be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=1\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487857} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f6d5db-d453-51b2-81bf-72bad96c4aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=0\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487905} {:answer/id #uuid "c14e4e69-3b50-5f9c-aab3-933c64469cdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487932} {:answer/id #uuid "c152b716-01ac-5012-a5ba-cb9700cb7912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=1\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487933} {:answer/id #uuid "c8035750-8d78-5097-9367-a314cfe52d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=0\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c14e4e69-3b50-5f9c-aab3-933c64469cdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sup(A)=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487932} :answer-field/id #uuid "afd78a1e-c9e7-53fa-8911-aad04834878d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d021d0f6-fbf3-5eed-804d-eee551071be6" :question/math-academy-id "q-253911" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{(-1)^{n}\\cdot (n-1)\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=(-1)^{n}\\cdot (n-1),\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/58/5812e3dd22994d613ecc84087418cddfa978e98c1324869f290e1bf2b1317bad.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is an oscillating, non-convergent sequence. Moreover, $A$ is unbounded above. In other words, for any real number $x,$ we can always find a sufficiently large $n$ such that ${a}_{n}$ is greater than $x.$ Therefore, $A$ has no upper bounds and $sup(A)=+\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162157 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fee0e08c-5a7a-5f78-83aa-39679bb3b17b" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08cd6155-dc0e-5bb2-b7f3-1d43209995e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #e