type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487845} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe05856-47c3-5f10-b2b7-1e438304a212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "933bb0d2-6ec2-5649-82b7-5a6987cdadb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487845} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc20f825-6c6e-54ea-a9f9-75910082951a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fd389a5-7049-5019-81b0-f04bbd0ca8ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487693} {:answer/id #uuid "873bb01d-c51c-5a28-9714-1be8eb59e277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487822} {:answer/id #uuid "b93fb8d2-9112-5548-99a4-f156ce9be7ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487916} {:answer/id #uuid "d702c1d2-8718-5e9f-b6a9-f8cec2dc39b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fd389a5-7049-5019-81b0-f04bbd0ca8ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487693} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec61e723-576f-5d4c-9b8c-8c68fc8a3aaf" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3734deb0-c791-5999-b0aa-dbef4240fdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487673} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce4e8eb-5308-5d7a-a1f9-c3552f8495a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487681} {:answer/id #uuid "886afc4d-e66c-5812-a260-a3ec7d3a61f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487828} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf52883-ed79-514b-ab30-628dfe55ba7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded above" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3734deb0-c791-5999-b0aa-dbef4240fdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded below" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487673} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0db6243-3349-5558-9574-70fe3060bd88" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "506b27d0-9ecb-54b1-8cb0-ba21f98fbff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-343939" :question/problem "Consider the set $B=(-\\infty ,\\sqrt{2}\\,].$ Complete the following reasoning to determine $inf(B)$ and $sup(B).$\n\nThe infimum of $B$ is the {{field-1}} of $B,$ and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $B.$\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-3}}, we have $inf(B)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $B$ is {{field-5}}, we have $sup(B)$ {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B,$ and the supremum is the smallest upper bound of $B.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSince $B$ is unbounded below, $B$ has no lower bounds, so $inf(B)=-\\infty .$\n\nNext, to find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $B$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge \\sqrt{2}$ is greater than or equal to the elements of $B.$ Thus, the set $[\\sqrt{2},\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $B.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<\\sqrt{2}$ is **not** an upper bound of $B.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $B$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $[\\sqrt{2},\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $B,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(B)=min\\,[\\sqrt{2},\\infty )=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of a set $B$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $B,$ and the supremum is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $B.$\n\nSince $B$ is $\\text{unbounded below},$ we have $inf(B)=-\\infty .$\n\nSince $B$ is $\\text{bounded above},$ we have $sup(B)=\\sqrt{2}.$"}]}
